WEBVTT

00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:11.301
GRINDELWALD: So...

00:00:15.055 --> 00:00:16.890
Credence Barebone.

00:00:19.059 --> 00:00:22.270
Nearly destroyed
by the woman who raised him.

00:00:23.105 --> 00:00:25.774
Yet now he seeks
the mother who bore him.

00:00:26.776 --> 00:00:28.610
He's desperate for family.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.321
He's desperate for love.

00:00:32.782 --> 00:00:35.492
He's the key to our victory.

00:00:36.368 --> 00:00:38.077
We know where the boy is, don't we?

00:00:39.622 --> 00:00:42.957
- Why don't we grab him and leave?
- He must come to me freely,

00:00:43.626 --> 00:00:44.793
and he will.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:50.006
The path has been laid,
and he is following it.

00:00:52.384 --> 00:00:54.594
The trail that will lead him to me

00:00:55.387 --> 00:00:59.098
and the strange and glorious truth
of who he is.

00:00:59.266 --> 00:01:00.975
KRALL: Why is he so important?

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:12.612
Who represents the greatest threat
to our cause?

00:01:13.614 --> 00:01:15.198
Albus Dumbledore.

00:01:15.699 --> 00:01:17.450
If I asked you now

00:01:17.618 --> 00:01:21.579
to go to the school where he is hiding
and kill him for me,

00:01:21.747 --> 00:01:23.498
would you do it for me, Krall?

00:01:29.839 --> 00:01:32.257
Credence is the only entity alive

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.593
who can kill him.

00:01:37.429 --> 00:01:39.138
You really think
he can kill the Great...

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.935
Can kill Albus Dumbledore?

00:01:44.728 --> 00:01:46.813
I know he can.

00:01:47.439 --> 00:01:51.401
But will you be with us
when that happens, Krall?

00:01:54.572 --> 00:01:55.780
Will you?

00:02:08.085 --> 00:02:10.003
NEWT: Jacob, that man
Tina's been seeing...

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:13.506
JACOB: Don't worry. She's gonna see you,
and she'll see the four of us together,

00:02:13.674 --> 00:02:15.550
it'll be just like New York
all over again. Don't worry about it.

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:16.843
NEWT: Yes, but he's an Auror,
Queenie said.

00:02:17.011 --> 00:02:19.262
JACOB: Yeah, he's an Auror. So what?
Don't worry about him.

00:02:22.558 --> 00:02:25.393
What do you think
I should say to her if I see her?

00:02:26.937 --> 00:02:30.607
Oh, well, it's best
not to plan these things.

00:02:31.233 --> 00:02:34.444
You know, you just say
whatever comes to you in the moment.

00:02:38.782 --> 00:02:41.492
She has eyes just like a salamander.

00:02:42.536 --> 00:02:43.703
Don't say that.

00:02:47.499 --> 00:02:50.376
Look, (CLEARS THROAT)
you just tell her that you missed her.

00:02:50.544 --> 00:02:51.961
- Right.
- Right, and then,

00:02:52.129 --> 00:02:54.964
you came all the way to Paris
just to find her.

00:02:55.591 --> 00:02:57.800
She'll love that. And then,

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:01.930
tell her you're losing sleep at night
for thinking of her and...

00:03:03.474 --> 00:03:05.433
Just don't say nothing about
no salamanders, all right?

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:06.601
- Okay.
- Okay.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:08.519
Hey. Hey, hey.

00:03:10.272 --> 00:03:11.522
It's gonna be all right.

00:03:11.899 --> 00:03:13.191
We're in this together, pal.

00:03:13.692 --> 00:03:15.735
Okay, I'm gonna help you out.
I'm gonna help you find Tina,

00:03:16.111 --> 00:03:17.362
find Queenie,

00:03:18.238 --> 00:03:20.198
and we'll all be happy again,
just like old times.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.407
Who is this guy?

00:03:23.452 --> 00:03:26.663
NEWT: Oh, he's the only way I can
leave the country without documentation.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:29.290
Now, you don't suffer from
motion sickness, do you?

00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:31.501
I don't do well on boats, Newt.

00:03:32.294 --> 00:03:33.378
You'll be fine.

00:03:33.462 --> 00:03:35.546
PORTKEY TOUT: Stir your stumps.
Leaves in one minute.

00:03:37.132 --> 00:03:38.132
50 Galleons.

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:39.384
No, we said 30.

00:03:39.468 --> 00:03:41.469
Uh-huh. 30 to go to France.

00:03:41.804 --> 00:03:43.513
20 not to tell anyone

00:03:43.597 --> 00:03:46.724
I seen Newt Scamander
leaving the country illegally.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:49.811
Price of fame, pal.

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:56.150
Mmm. Ten seconds.

00:03:56.318 --> 00:03:58.361
- Eight.
- Jacob.

00:03:58.445 --> 00:03:59.612
Seven.

00:04:00.864 --> 00:04:01.948
Six.

00:04:02.866 --> 00:04:03.866
Mmm...

00:04:04.994 --> 00:04:06.119
Four.

00:04:06.954 --> 00:04:08.955
Three. Two.

00:04:09.957 --> 00:04:11.207
One.

00:04:12.459 --> 00:04:13.876
(JACOB SCREAMING)

00:04:20.676 --> 00:04:22.427
(GROANS) I didn't like
that Portkey, Newt.

00:04:22.594 --> 00:04:24.012
So you keep saying.

00:04:24.555 --> 00:04:25.805
Follow me.

00:04:25.889 --> 00:04:27.306
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATION)

00:04:32.563 --> 00:04:33.563
<i>Confundus.</i>

00:04:34.189 --> 00:04:35.690
(HICCUPING DRUNKENLY)

00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:37.483
- (GIGGLING)
- (JACOB LAUGHS)

00:04:37.568 --> 00:04:38.609
(SHUSHES)

00:04:38.694 --> 00:04:40.319
NEWT: Come on.
It'll wear off in a few minutes.

00:04:41.905 --> 00:04:43.072
(HICCUPS)

00:04:43.157 --> 00:04:44.532
(GIGGLING)

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:54.375
<i>Appare Vestigium.</i>

00:04:59.757 --> 00:05:00.798
Accio Niffler.

00:05:02.009 --> 00:05:03.259
Get looking.

00:05:03.594 --> 00:05:05.136
Oi! Get looking!

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.766
That's a Kappa.

00:05:10.768 --> 00:05:12.310
It's a Japanese water demon.

00:05:17.232 --> 00:05:18.399
Tina?

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:20.151
Tina!

00:05:26.867 --> 00:05:28.409
What have you found?

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.040
JACOB: And we're licking the dirt now.

00:05:40.714 --> 00:05:42.548
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

00:05:48.222 --> 00:05:49.555
<i>Revelio.</i>

00:05:52.101 --> 00:05:54.227
Newt, what made those?

00:05:54.812 --> 00:05:56.187
That is a Zouwu.

00:05:58.816 --> 00:06:00.525
It's a Chinese creature.

00:06:00.692 --> 00:06:02.860
They are incredibly fast
and incredibly powerful.

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:05.363
They can travel 1,000 miles in a day,

00:06:05.906 --> 00:06:08.157
and this one could take you
from one part of Paris to the next

00:06:08.242 --> 00:06:09.283
in a single leap.

00:06:09.952 --> 00:06:11.160
(NIFFLER CHITTERING)

00:06:13.163 --> 00:06:14.413
NEWT: Oh, good boy.

00:06:16.125 --> 00:06:17.583
Jacob, she was here.

00:06:18.293 --> 00:06:19.585
Tina stood here.

00:06:19.962 --> 00:06:22.004
She has incredibly narrow feet.
Have you noticed?

00:06:24.174 --> 00:06:25.758
Can't say that I have.

00:06:29.721 --> 00:06:31.264
Then someone came towards her.

00:06:39.273 --> 00:06:41.190
(SNIFFING)

00:06:43.277 --> 00:06:44.610
<i>Avensegium.</i>

00:06:49.283 --> 00:06:50.908
- Right. Follow that feather.
- What?

00:06:51.076 --> 00:06:52.702
- Jacob, follow the feather.
- Follow the feather.

00:06:53.453 --> 00:06:54.787
Where is he?

00:06:55.789 --> 00:06:56.831
Accio Niffler.

00:07:04.298 --> 00:07:05.715
Drop the bucket.

